# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database (server-only) — required. MongoDB Atlas.
# Prisma does not support `prisma migrate` on MongoDB, so the schema is applied
# with `db push` instead: npm run db:deploy
# The database name MUST appear in the connection string. Prisma reads only the
# URL and has no separate "db name" setting, so a URI without the /dbname path
# fails with "Database must be defined in the connection string". This is worth
# checking first: the variable can be present and still be unusable, which looks
# identical to "the database is unreachable" from the admin panel.
# After changing this in Vercel you must redeploy; the value is read at runtime,
# not baked into the build.
# Local dev example:
#   mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@cluster0.xxxx.mongodb.net/natures_choice?appName=Cluster0
# MONGODB_URI=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Razorpay — required for checkout.
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_ID     server-only, Test mode key while developing
#   RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET server-only, never exposed to the browser
# The key id is sent to the browser in the create-order response, so there is no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID. Do not add one: a second copy can drift.
# A rzp_live_ key takes real money. Use Test keys until you intend real payments.
# Test keys: https://dashboard.razorpay.com/app/keys  (mode: Test)
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Order signing (server-only) — required.
# Signs admin session cookies and customer receipt links.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# Falls back to AUTH_SECRET, then RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET if unset.
# ORDER_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin login (server-only) — required to reach /admin.
# ADMIN_EMAIL is the login handle; ADMIN_PASSWORD must be >= 8 characters.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shipping (server-only) — the cart never sends amounts; these drive pricing.
# SHIPPING_FEE_INR=49
# Optional: waive delivery above this order subtotal (blank = always charge).
# FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD_INR=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# App
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://hero-pi-seven.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=8805551680

# Cloudinary (server-only)
# NOT CURRENTLY READ BY THE APPLICATION. There is no upload or delete code in
# src/ and no cloudinary package in package.json. Product images are static
# files under public/ referenced from src/lib/products.ts. Set these only when
# that integration is actually built.
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# Delhivery (server-only)
# NOT CURRENTLY READ BY THE APPLICATION. There is no shipment, tracking or
# delivery-status code in src/. The admin Delivery page reads only the shipping
# fee variables above.
# DELHIVERY_API_KEY=
# DELHIVERY_BASE_URL=
# DELHIVERY_CLIENT_ID=

# Contact webhook (server-only) — only used by /api/contact. The contact form
# itself now hands off to WhatsApp and does not post here.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Analytics (server-only) — not currently read by the application.
# META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Diagnosing a database problem
# GET /api/admin/db-health (requires an admin session) performs a real ping and
# reports the host, the database name in use, the server version and the
# collections it can see. It never returns the connection string or credentials.
# The Overview and Orders pages show the same classified reason when a query
# fails, so an unreachable database is never presented as a set of zeros.

# Auth (server-only) — fallback for ORDER_SIGNING_SECRET
AUTH_SECRET=
